Example 7 Find $\lim _{x \rightarrow+\infty} \frac{3 x+5}{6 x-8}$.
Solution. Divide each term in the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ that occurs in the denominator, namely, $x^{1}=x$. We obtain

$$
